{"t": 1794108179.4471786, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_reply_to_pull_request_comment", "args": {"body": "Done - renamed the parameter to `amount_cents` in the signature and used it for the returned value, so the unit is explicit at the call site too. The dict key was already `amount_cents`. No other file in the repo calls `make_entry` with `amt=` as a keyword, so nothing else needed updating.", "commentId": 90011, "owner": "acme", "pullNumber": 88, "repo": "ledger"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794108181.0835352, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_reply_to_pull_request_comment", "args": {"body": "Done - `make_entry` now raises `ValueError(\"amount_cents must be non-negative\")` when `amount_cents < 0`, so refunds can't sneak in as negative entries; zero is still accepted. Refund handling is left to the separate entry type you mentioned - that type doesn't exist in this repo yet, so I didn't add any refund path here.", "commentId": 90012, "owner": "acme", "pullNumber": 88, "repo": "ledger"}, "ok": true}
